# do not delete me
#
# Git tracks files, not directories, so this directory would vanish from
# the next clone without a file in it. This is that file. It ignores
# nothing on purpose — see `keepMarker` in schemas/cat-harness.ts.
#
# library/
# L1 source content — one <bib-slug>/ per ingested document, holding
# sections/*.md, structure.json and, where the source was scanned,
# ocr/page-NNN.txt. Every knowledge-graph reference to a source resolves
# THROUGH here, never to a loose path or a bare URL.
#
# ── THIS ONE IS EMPTY, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE ──────────────────────────
#
# Bean `frs5` moved all four entries out on 2026-09-20 — the three IRIS
# items to `who-iris/library/`, `milnorlink` to `folio-assistant-sci/library/`
# — because the platform holds no content. This marker went with them and
# the declaration went with it.
#
# Both came back, on the owner's ruling the same day, for ONE reason and it
# is not about this instance: `wwi6` pins the guarantee that a DEPENDENT
# folio materialises its own `uploads/` and `library/`, and a dependent
# inherits that convention — an id and a relative path — from what the
# harness declares. Remove the declaration and every downstream folio
# silently stops getting a library; remove this file and `harness:dirs:check`
# reports a declared directory that is not there.
#
# It IS the `dh4f` shape: a declared directory holding nothing. That was
# weighed, not missed. The cost is bounded because the consumers that scan
# libraries now fan out over EVERY declared one (bean `a02m`), so this one
# contributes nothing rather than shadowing the two that have documents.
# What it must never become again is the FIRST of several, silently taken
# as the only one — which is what `[0]` did until that bean.
#
# The real fix is the core relocation: `uploads`, `voices`,
# `translation-sources` and `library` moving to folio-assistant-core, per
# the owner's "voices, uploads library in folio-asst-core". After that a
# dependent inherits them from the layer that owns content, and this
# directory goes for good.
